  "result": "The tests all pass, which validates the dashboard function works correctly. Here's a summary of the implementation:\n\n## Dashboard Function Summary\n\n**Implementation in `src/reports.js`:**\n\nThe `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function returns:\n\n1. **counts**: Number of invoices by status\n   - draft, issued, partially_paid, paid\n\n2. **outstanding**: Total amount still due\n   - Sums balance due on all 'issued' and 'partially_paid' invoices\n\n3. **overdue**: Object with count and total amount\n   - `count`: number of overdue invoices\n   - `amount`: total due on overdue invoices\n   - Uses the existing `overdueInvoices()` function\n\n4. **topCustomers**: Top 3 customers by outstanding amount\n   - Array of `[{ customerId, due }, ...]`\n   - Sorted highest due first\n   - Only includes 'issued' and 'partially_paid' invoices\n\n**Test Coverage (14 new tests):**\n\n\u2705 Empty invoices list\n\u2705 Counts invoices by status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n\u2705 Calculates outstanding amount correctly\n\u2705 Excludes draft and paid from outstanding\n\u2705 Calculates overdue invoices\n\u2705 Includes both count and amount for overdue\n\u2705 Finds top 3 customers by due amount\n\u2705 Limits topCustomers to 3\n\u2705 Topcustomers sorted highest first\n\u2705 Aggregates multiple invoices per customer\n\u2705 Includes paid in counts but not in outstanding\n\u2705 Handles partially paid invoices correctly\n\u2705 Empty topCustomers when none outstanding\n\u2705 Works with complex invoice mix\n\n**Test Results: 402/402 passing \u2713**",
